  "cv_caveat": "Accuracy is pooled out-of-fold over all rows, not a mean of folds. Group sizes are highly uneven (96/23/11/8/5/2), so per-fold accuracy on the smallest groups rests on very few samples; std_accuracy is not meaningful and marginal_spread support is 1-2 rows in three of five folds. StratifiedGroupKFold(group=report_id) yields only 2 distinct partitions across 200 seeds, so it is effectively leave-one-report-out and cannot be averaged over splitter seeds. Grouped accuracy slightly exceeds plain stratified accuracy because within-report neighbours are parametric-sweep siblings that straddle the extinction boundary: the nearest same-report neighbour agrees in label 55% of the time versus 62% for the nearest cross-report neighbour, so same-report training rows actively mislead. Most of the remaining gap is single-seed noise.",
